-- the regulations the in-scope provisions depend on: rr 5B, 5CA, 5CB, 7D, 7F, 7FA, 10AD, 10A, 11 and 12I.
-- Source: sources/rtr-1989.05-ad0-00.mrdoc_49840.txt (r 5B lines 149-184, r 5CA 185-191, r 5CB 192-204,
-- r 7D 318-327, r 7F 347-357, r 7FA 358-362, r 10AD 467-476, r 10A 477-479, r 11 480-482, r 12I 628-637).
-- Reference register REF-07, -24, -26, -28, -29, -31, -35, -37, -47, -72, -78, -80, -83.
-- Each regulation that disapplies or modifies a section is made under the Act's s 6; whether it is
-- within s 6 is not an input to any outcome (REF-85). LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`

§ `Regulation 5B -- Exemptions from section 30(1) of Act`

-- r 5B(2A)(a)-(c), (2), (3) and (4): s 30(1) does not apply to the agreement, the premises or the
-- agency. Who is a listed employer, a Government employee, an agency in the Tables and so on are
-- facts (REF-36).
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 5B(2A), (2), (3), (4)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 5B -- section 30(1) does not apply to` a IF
        "(2A)(a) employer in the Table, employee a tenant" ... a's `status`'s `the lessor is an employer in the Table to r 5B(2A) and a tenant is its employee`
    ..  "(2A)(b) Housing Authority or a Department, premises let to a Government employee" ... a's `status`'s `the lessor is the Housing Authority or a GEHA department and the premises are let to a Government employee under the GEHA`
    ..  "(2A)(c) WA Country Health Service" ... a's `status`'s `the lessor is the WA Country Health Service and a tenant is employed or engaged by it`
    ..  "(2) Butler's Cottage" ... a's `status`'s `the premises are Butler's Cottage, Government House`
    ..  "(3) agencies in the Table" ... a's `status`'s `the lessor is an agency in the Table to r 5B(3)`
    OR  "(4) the Crown as lessor, an officer of a department in the Table a tenant" ... a's `status`'s `the Crown is the lessor and a tenant is an officer of a department in the Table to r 5B(4)`

§ `Regulation 5CA -- Modified application of section 30(2)(a) of Act`

-- r 5CA(1)(b): the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2011 s 27(2) came into operation on 1 July
-- 2013 (a fact taken from the compilation table, REF-38).
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 5CA(1)(b); reference register REF-38
`the day the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2011 s 27(2) came into operation` MEANS `day number` 2013 7 1

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 5CA(1)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 5CA -- applies to` a IF
        "(a) creates a tenancy for a fixed term" ... a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND "(b) was entered into before" ... a's `entered into on` LESS THAN `the day the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2011 s 27(2) came into operation`

-- r 5CA(2): s 30(2)(a) applies as if its condition read "the agreement provides that the rent may
-- increase or be increased" instead of "the amount of the increase, or the method of calculating the
-- amount of the increase, is set out in the agreement".
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 30(2)(a); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 5CA(2)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2)(a), as modified by r 5CA where it applies -- the agreement allows an increase during the term` a IF
    IF `r 5CA -- applies to` a
    THEN "the agreement provides that the rent may increase or be increased" ... a's `provides that the rent may increase`
    ELSE "the amount of the increase, or the method of calculating the amount of the increase, is set out in the agreement" ... a's `the amount or method of an increase is set out`

§ `Regulation 5CB -- Modified application of Act s. 31`

-- r 5CB(b): s 31(1AA), the relevant events on which the lessor may increase the security bond.
-- Made under s 6(b) for premises, with no class named: it applies to all premises.
DECLARE `Event that may support a bond increase` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor gives the tenant a notice of increase of rent under s 30 or 31A` HAS
        `the rent increase takes effect on` IS A NUMBER
    `the lessor gives notice approving a request to keep a pet under s 50B(4)`
    `the lessor is taken to approve a request to keep a pet under s 50B(5)`
    `the Commissioner gives notice of an order to consent to keeping a pet under s 50E(2)(b) or 50G(2)(a)`
    `some other event`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 31(1A), (1AA); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 5CB(a), (b)
GIVEN e IS AN `Event that may support a bond increase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 5CB -- s 31(1AA) -- is a relevant event` e IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the lessor gives the tenant a notice of increase of rent under s 30 or 31A` d THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the lessor gives notice approving a request to keep a pet under s 50B(4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the lessor is taken to approve a request to keep a pet under s 50B(5)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Commissioner gives notice of an order to consent to keeping a pet under s 50E(2)(b) or 50G(2)(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some other event` THEN FALSE

-- r 5CB(c): s 31(1B)(b) as modified: "if a notice of increase of rent is given to the tenant under
-- section 30 or 31A -- before the rent increase the subject of the notice" takes effect. The day
-- before which the additional bond cannot be payable, if any.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 31(1B)(b); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 5CB(c)
GIVEN e IS AN `Event that may support a bond increase`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`r 5CB -- s 31(1B)(b) -- the day the rent increase takes effect, if the event is a rent notice` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the lessor gives the tenant a notice of increase of rent under s 30 or 31A` d THEN JUST d
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 7D -- Modified application of section 70A of Act for Foyer Oxford`

-- r 7D(2)(a): a fixed term "of 6 weeks or less". The fixed term runs from the day the tenancy
-- commences to the expiry day, both included (Interpretation Act s 61(1)(a), (d)).
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7D(2)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 7D -- applies to` a IF
        "(a) a residential unit in Foyer Oxford ... (c) entered into between a tenant and Foundation Housing Limited"
    ... a's `status`'s `the premises are a residential unit in Foyer Oxford and the agreement is with Foundation Housing Limited`
    AND "(a) for a fixed term of 6 weeks or less"
    ... (CONSIDER `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST e THEN (e MINUS a's `tenancy commenced on` PLUS 1) AT MOST 42)
    AND "(b) is not the renewal or extension of an agreement"
    ... NOT a's `status`'s `the agreement is the renewal or extension of an agreement`

-- r 7D(3): s 70A(3) applies as if "30 days" read "7 days".
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(3); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7D(3)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` a MEANS
    IF `r 7D -- applies to` a THEN 7 ELSE 30

§ `Regulation 7F -- Exemptions from Act s. 82`

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7F(a), (b)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` a IF
        "(a)" ... a's `status`'s `the Housing Authority is a party, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting`
    OR  "(b)" ... a's `status`'s `the WA Country Health Service is the tenant, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting to its staff`

§ `Regulation 7FA -- Modified application of Act s. 85 for Housing Authority`

-- r 7FA(2): s 85(1)(ba) inserted: if the Housing Authority gives the notice in relation to premises of
-- which it is the lessor, it may be given by leaving it at the premises.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 85(1); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7FA
GIVEN g IS A `Giving of a notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 7FA -- s 85(1)(ba) -- the notice may be left at the premises` g IF
    g's `the Housing Authority is the lessor and gives it`

§ `Regulation 10AD -- Amount prescribed for section 27(2)(a) of Act`

-- The Table's rows overlap: an agreement for premises south of the 26th parallel at a weekly rent of
-- $1 200 or more matches row 2 ("exceeds $500", $100) and row 3 ($1 200). Fork FK-14.
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 10AD, Table row 1
GIVEN `weekly rent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 10AD -- row 1 describes an agreement at weekly rent` `weekly rent` IF
    "Where the weekly rent ... is $500 or less" ... `weekly rent` AT MOST 500

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 10AD, Table row 2
GIVEN `weekly rent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 10AD -- row 2 describes an agreement at weekly rent` `weekly rent` IF
    "Where the weekly rent ... exceeds $500" ... `weekly rent` GREATER THAN 500

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 10AD, Table row 3
GIVEN `weekly rent` IS A NUMBER, `south of the 26th parallel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 10AD -- row 3 describes an agreement at weekly rent` `weekly rent` `south of the 26th parallel:` `south of the 26th parallel` IF
        "for residential premises south of the 26th parallel of south latitude" ... `south of the 26th parallel`
    AND "and the weekly rent is $1 200 or more" ... `weekly rent` AT LEAST 1200

-- FK-14, reading taken (A): the amount prescribed is the greatest amount opposite any row that
-- describes the agreement (s 27(2)(a) speaks of "a prescribed amount"; row 3 is the specific row).
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 10AD; Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27(2)(a); fork FK-14 reading A
GIVEN `weekly rent` IS A NUMBER, `south of the 26th parallel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`r 10AD -- the amount prescribed for s 27(2)(a), at weekly rent` `weekly rent` `south of the 26th parallel:` `south of the 26th parallel` MEANS
    IF `r 10AD -- row 3 describes an agreement at weekly rent` `weekly rent` `south of the 26th parallel:` `south of the 26th parallel`
    THEN 1200
    ELSE IF `r 10AD -- row 2 describes an agreement at weekly rent` `weekly rent`
         THEN 100
         ELSE 50

-- FK-14, reading rejected (B): where two rows describe the agreement, the lesser amount governs
-- (an amount must not exceed the amount opposite every description that fits the agreement).
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 10AD; fork FK-14 reading B
GIVEN `weekly rent` IS A NUMBER, `south of the 26th parallel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`FK-14 reading B -- r 10AD -- the amount prescribed, at weekly rent` `weekly rent` `south of the 26th parallel:` `south of the 26th parallel` MEANS
    IF `r 10AD -- row 2 describes an agreement at weekly rent` `weekly rent`
    THEN 100
    ELSE 50

§ `Regulation 10A -- Amount prescribed for section 29(1)(b)(ii) of Act`

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 10A
`r 10A -- the amount prescribed for s 29(1)(b)(ii)` MEANS 350

§ `Regulation 11 -- Amount prescribed for section 29(2) of Act`

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 11
`r 11 -- the amount prescribed for s 29(2)` MEANS 1200

§ `Regulation 12I -- Prescribed circumstances and prescribed electronic means for Act s. 85(1)(c)`

@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 12I(1) "authorised notice"
GIVEN g IS A `Giving of a notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 12I(1) -- the notice is an authorised notice` g IF
    g's `kind of notice` EQUALS `an authorised notice (r 12I(1))`

-- r 12I(2)(a): the other prescribed circumstances in which an authorised notice may be given by
-- prescribed electronic means.
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 12I(2)(a)
GIVEN g IS A `Giving of a notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 12I(2)(a) -- prescribed circumstances exist for` g IF
        `r 12I(1) -- the notice is an authorised notice` g
    AND "the email address of the person has been provided to the bond administrator together with (i) a record of the payment of a bond ... or (ii) a security bond release application"
    ... g's `the recipient's email was given to the bond administrator with a bond record or release application`

-- r 12I(2)(b): "the prescribed electronic means by which an authorised notice may be given to or
-- served on a person is by sending the notice by email". No electronic means is prescribed for any
-- other notice. Fork FK-12 asks what that means for an in-scope notice sent by email with consent.
@ref Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 12I(2)(b)
GIVEN g IS A `Giving of a notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 12I(2)(b) -- email is a prescribed electronic means for` g IF
        g's `way` EQUALS `by email (s 85(1)(c))`
    AND `r 12I(1) -- the notice is an authorised notice` g
